    "definition": "observation.state (16) = [q1..q6 (rad, UR order, as observed -- see the joint_state_alignment note: the recorder's joint cache is stale by a per-take tau_q of ~0.9 s, so the joints are read at master_time + tau_q, by LINEAR INTERPOLATION of the joint record because that record ticks at a jittery ~63-67 Hz and nearest-neighbour would inject fake zero and fake double steps into the finite-difference action), tcp_x, tcp_y, tcp_z (m, base_link frame), r11, r21, r31, r12, r22, r32 (the first two COLUMNS of the TCP rotation matrix -- the continuous 6-D rotation representation, used because the carrot TCP sits ~175 deg from identity where a rotation vector would wrap), grip_pos (0=open..1=closed)]. TCP = ur_kin.fk(q) (base_link -> tool0 flange) translated by +0.174 m along the flange +Z. action (7) = [dx, dy, dz, drx, dry, drz, grip_cmd]: for dataset frame t on the 30 fps master clock, dp = p_tcp(q_{t+1}) - p_tcp(q_t) and drot = so3_log(R_tcp(q_{t+1}) @ R_tcp(q_t)^T), both expressed in the base frame with the rotation LEFT-multiplied; the last frame of every episode has dp = drot = 0. grip_cmd is the ABSOLUTE recorded gripper command (0=open..1=closed), ffill/bfill'd then resampled onto the master clock. The action is the ACHIEVED motion between consecutive frames, never the recorded `command` stream (which leads the measured joints by ~0.9 s in this session). Deploy inverts it exactly: p_target = p_live + dp, R_target = so3_exp(drot) @ R_live, then analytic IK with branch locking (eef_space.apply_delta / ik_tcp_nearest). Nothing here is scaled, clipped or filtered -- clamps belong to the deploy node only.",
